Subject: CPMS I03 No-Resolution Validator Threat Model

@ [threat_model_uuid] 705910e7-5e3a-435b-b9ac-b905fb54f38d
@ [profile] C:\Project\Cantor\specifications\CPMS_I03_Residual_Conformance_Profile.sop

& [ProtectedAssets] are local integrity availability confidentiality and deterministic replay
  + exact signed canonical schema bytes and their I02 bundle identity
  + supplied instance bytes and bounded normalized observations
  + local files credentials environment registry services network and process state
  + finite CPU memory diagnostic and reference budgets

& [AdversaryInput] includes every untrusted schema instance and diagnostic string at the I03 boundary
  + a canonical schema is trusted only after exact path byte length digest root identity dialect direction and bundle reconstruction pass
  + an instance never becomes trusted merely by parsing schema acceptance serde decoding or semantic evaluation

& [ThreatClasses] are explicit
  + remote reference retrieval can produce SSRF credential disclosure nondeterministic content and unbounded latency
  + file reference retrieval can disclose local data and convert filesystem state into hidden schema authority
  + registry environment and caller-supplied loaders can reintroduce ambient authority despite disabled default network features
  + recursive or adversarial references can exhaust compilation or validation resources
  + unbounded diagnostic rendering can amplify hostile strings or disclose internal paths
  + cached remote content can create replay disagreement even when a later run is offline

& [CompileTimeAbsence] is a necessary gate
  + Cargo uses exact jsonschema 0.49.2 with default-features false
  + the resolved feature graph contains none of resolve-http resolve-file tls-aws-lc-rs or any feature that installs an external retriever
  + the lock and cargo metadata prove zero HTTP TLS async transport packages within the added graph
  + source review names every custom-build crate and rejects unexpected native links code generation downloads or environment-derived behavior
  + absence is re-proved after every dependency update; semver compatibility is not sufficient

& [RuntimeAbsence] is independently necessary
  + Cantor constructs only an explicit Draft 2020-12 validator from admitted in-memory canonical bytes
  + Cantor installs no retriever registry resource cache callback or caller-provided resolver
  + a preflight graph walk rejects every reference that is not an internal fragment resolving within the same admitted document
  + schema compilation occurs only after the complete reference walk succeeds atomically
  + network file environment registry subprocess provider and persistence counters remain structurally absent from the I03 report type

& [ReferencePreflight] is syntax preserving
  + recursively visit object and array positions capable of containing schema resources
  + classify every $ref $dynamicRef $schema and identifier-bearing keyword according to Draft 2020-12 semantics rather than string search
  + permit the exact Draft 2020-12 dialect URI only in the root $schema field
  + permit fragment-only references whose JSON Pointer or anchor target resolves inside the same document
  + reject absolute relative file HTTP HTTPS opaque empty-base dynamic external or unresolved targets before validator construction
  + cap visited nodes references pointer segments decoded bytes and cycle work with checked arithmetic
  + preserve location keyword raw target and refusal class in a bounded observation

& [MetaSchemaDelineation] avoids hidden retrieval
  + use the validator library's embedded selected-draft meta-schema facility
  + do not interpret a document's own $schema value as permission to retrieve a dialect
  + meta-schema validation compile success and instance validation are three separate observations

& [DenialTests] are required
  * HTTP HTTPS file relative path UNC drive-letter data and unknown-scheme references
  * internal missing pointer invalid escaping excessive pointer depth and reference cycles
  * dynamic-reference forms that could escape the local resource
  * caller attempt to install a retriever or resource registry
  * environment proxy cache and current-directory variation producing identical refusal
  * report inspection proving zero external request file-open provider subprocess and persistence events

& [ResidualRisk] remains
  + third-party parser and validator defects can still consume resources or misclassify Draft semantics
  + compiled dependency build scripts execute at build time even when runtime resolution is absent
  + Windows Application Control currently blocks one required build helper and therefore prevents release proof
  + process sandboxing may add defense in depth later but is not a substitute for capability absence

& [AcceptanceRule] no-resolution passes only when compile graph source construction preflight denial corpus counters and exact replay all agree
  - never: infer no-resolution from offline mode alone
  - never: infer safety from absence of an observed request in one happy-path test
